Chapter: NetKeyHashTest
  cites Net chapter LoadBalancer
  cites Net chapter MessageQueue
  cites Foreword chapter ConsistentHash
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The first arm either of these chapters has had. `LoadBalancer` is cited by
 one chapter and `MessageQueue` by none, so both compile in a sweep and
 neither has ever been RUN; a text key reaching a partition or a backend was
 a claim nothing checked.

 THE VALUES ARE THE ASSERTION, not the shape. Both chapters turn a Text key
 into an Integer with the same djb2 fold and feed `chr-hash-key`, and this
 pins what that produces for five keys. It exists to be run either side of
 lifting the fold into `chr-hash-text`: identical numbers before and after
 are what says the lift changed nothing, and a fold that differs in its seed,
 its multiplier or its wrap moves every line below.

 The keys are chosen so a hash that ignored part of its input still fails:
 "a" and "b" differ in one byte, "ab" and "ba" are a transposition, and
 "abc" against "abcabc" is a repeat that a fold without a multiply would
 collapse.

Section: Fixtures

  four : Integer = 4

  keys : List Text = ["a", "b", "ab", "ba", "abc"]

  pool0 : BackendPool
  pool0 =
    let p1 = pool-add (pool-new "web" LbConsistentHash) (backend-new "one" "10.0.0.1" 80)
    in let p2 = pool-add p1 (backend-new "two" "10.0.0.2" 80)
    in let p3 = pool-add p2 (backend-new "three" "10.0.0.3" 80)
    in pool-add p3 (backend-new "four" "10.0.0.4" 80)

Section: Helpers

  parts : List Text, Integer, Text -> Text
  parts (ks) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ks then acc
    else parts ks (i + 1) (acc & " " & show (tp-hash-partition (list-at ks i) four))

  picks : List Text, Integer, Text -> Text
  picks (ks) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length ks then acc
    else picks ks (i + 1) (acc & " " & pick-of (list-at ks i))

  pick-of : Text -> Text
  pick-of (k) =
    when pool-select pool0 k
      is None -> "none"
      is Just (id) -> id

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("net-key partition" & parts keys 0 "")
    print-line-uni ("net-key backend" & picks keys 0 "")
  end
